    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Analyze a local media file and return material understanding metadata.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --path, --input TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Input media file path; audio is supported by speech modules.\r\n          --prompt TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Material understanding prompt.\r\n          --asset-id TEXT     Stable Blueprint resource asset_id.\r\n          --material-id TEXT  Original material id from the caller.\r\n          --segment-id TEXT   Optional draft segment id when the caller analyzes a segment.\r\n          --type TEXT [asset]  \r\n                              Understanding source type. Default: asset.\r\n          --start-time TEXT   Start time for media analysis. Explicit unit required: us, ms, s,\r\n                              or min.\r\n          --duration TEXT     Analysis duration. Explicit unit required: us, ms, s, or min;\r\n                              omit for implementation default.\r\n          --frame-interval <duration> [1s] \r\n                              Frame sampling interval. Explicit unit required: us, ms, s, or\r\n                              min.\r\n          --analysis-level TEXT \r\n                              Optional analysis level forwarded to the understanding\r\n                              implementation.\r\n          --analysis-module TEXT:{visual-content,speech-transcript,speech-analysis,face-body-detection} ... \r\n                              Analysis module. Repeatable.\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  $ lyra-cli media understand --path /tmp/clip.mp4 --prompt \"analyze the main subjects and visual style\"\r\n  $ lyra-cli media understand --path /tmp/clip.mp4 --prompt \"describe the subjects and scene\" --analysis-module visual-content\r\n\r\nNOTES\r\n  - --path is the local media path to analyze.\r\n  - --prompt is handled by videoeditor MaterialUnderstandingService.\r\n  - Modules: visual-content, speech-transcript, speech-analysis, face-body-detection.\r\n  - Audio inputs support speech-transcript and speech-analysis only.\r\n  - Time fields accept explicit units: us, ms, s, or min.\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
      "output": "Analyze a local media file and return material understanding metadata.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --path, --input TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Input media file path; audio is supported by speech modules.\r\n          --prompt TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Material understanding prompt.\r\n          --asset-id TEXT     Stable Blueprint resource asset_id.\r\n          --material-id TEXT  Original material id from the caller.\r\n          --segment-id TEXT   Optional draft segment id when the caller analyzes a segment.\r\n          --type TEXT [asset]  \r\n                              Understanding source type. Default: asset.\r\n          --start-time TEXT   Start time for media analysis. Explicit unit required: us, ms, s,\r\n                              or min.\r\n          --duration TEXT     Analysis duration. Explicit unit required: us, ms, s, or min;\r\n                              omit for implementation default.\r\n          --frame-interval <duration> [1s] \r\n                              Frame sampling interval. Explicit unit required: us, ms, s, or\r\n                              min.\r\n          --analysis-level TEXT \r\n                              Optional analysis level forwarded to the understanding\r\n                              implementation.\r\n          --analysis-module TEXT:{visual-content,speech-transcript,speech-analysis,face-body-detection} ... \r\n                              Analysis module. Repeatable.\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  $ lyra-cli media understand --path /tmp/clip.mp4 --prompt \"analyze the main subjects and visual style\"\r\n  $ lyra-cli media understand --path /tmp/clip.mp4 --prompt \"describe the subjects and scene\" --analysis-module visual-content\r\n\r\nNOTES\r\n  - --path is the local media path to analyze.\r\n  - --prompt is handled by videoeditor MaterialUnderstandingService.\r\n  - Modules: visual-content, speech-transcript, speech-analysis, face-body-detection.\r\n  - Audio inputs support speech-transcript and speech-analysis only.\r\n  - Time fields accept explicit units: us, ms, s, or min.\r\n",
